[464.736, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step report**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Did:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Rebuilt `mirror-twins.html` around a new core mechanic, **flip pads**. The orange twin's mirror rule is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  no longer fixed. Stepping onto a purple ⇄ pad flips its left–right rule, and a green ⇅ pad flips its up–down\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rule. Two badges show the current rule.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Replaced the 11 random levels with 16 in four chapters: Mirror, Flip, Pits and Axis. Each is picked from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a search for the tightest candidate, meaning fewest optimal solutions and fewest objects.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Added a title screen, a level map with stars against par, a share button, smooth sliding, sound and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  win burst. It also has swipe, on-screen arrows and keyboard controls.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Not built: custom-level sharing, since you said to skip it unless easy.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Found:** both checks you named pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Solver:** all 16 levels are solvable, and par equals the optimal move count. Every Flip and Axis level\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is unsolvable if its pads are treated as plain floor. Every Pits level is shorter without pits, so the pits\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  really constrain it. Nearly every level has a single optimal solution (a few have 2–3).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Real Chrome:** it played all 16 levels through actual keystrokes and won each one in exactly par\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  moves. There were zero console errors.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Look:** I checked the desktop and phone game screens and the title screen. The title tokens were\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  squashed into ovals, which I fixed. I did not re-view the title after the fix.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Not checked:** I haven't seen the phone level map. My screenshot sheet cut it off and I ran out of look\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rounds, so its layout is untested by eye. The game's feel (movement, sound) is also unjudged, since I can't\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  hear it or play it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Changed course:** the puzzle is no longer just mirrored movement, because a mirror-only game wasn't new\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  enough. The levels list is shorter and tighter. The 3-star rule is par or better, and 2 stars is within 40%\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  of par.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The build and check scripts are in `.ambition/tools/`. I saved a copy of the game to `.ambition/steps/3/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
