[484.635, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 4/8 · Challenge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions, riskiest first.** I'm listing who set each one and how I'll test it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **The page survives wherever you host it.** I assumed `localStorage` always works. I set that. On itch.io\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and in some Safari iframe modes, storage is blocked, and my code would crash on load. Test: load it with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  storage throwing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **The layout works on phones.** I assumed this and never saw the phone level map or a landscape phone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Test: render both.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Every level is a good puzzle.** I picked fewest-solutions plus fewest-objects as the quality proxy.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Test: measure soft-locks, whether each twin is needed, and how the difficulty ramps.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **Stars are fair.** I set the rule myself: 3 stars only for par, 2 within 140% of par. Test: count how\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  many near-par solutions exist.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  5. **Locking levels is good for you.** I assumed progressive unlock fits a portfolio game. Test: ask what an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  itch visitor sees in the first minute.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  6. **The Continue and win flow works.** I wrote it quickly. Test: drive it in Chrome.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  7. **The mechanic is original.** That is your target and I can't prove it. Test: a web search.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
