[595.661, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step report**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Did:** I tested each assumption against the running game, or against solver data, instead of reasoning\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  about it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Hosting: the game crashed when browser storage was blocked, as on itch.io iframes and some Safari modes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  It now loads and plays with storage blocked.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Phones: the portrait map and game are fine. The landscape-phone board was tiny, because the on-screen\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  arrows took the space. In short landscape the arrows now sit in a corner and the board grew from 128 to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  about 392 px wide.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Levels: unlocked all 16 (see below).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Win flow: Continue and Enter behave correctly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Soft-locks.** Many levels have positions where a win is impossible. Level 10 has 85 of its 155\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  reachable states like that. Players would have burned moves without knowing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **A real bug from the playthrough.** The previous level's win overlay could appear 380ms late and block\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  input on the next level. I fixed it. After the fix, three full runs of all 16 levels in Chrome had no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  failures and no console errors.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Stars are fair.** Every level has at least 64 solutions within 140% of par, except the first two and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  few pit levels, which still have 100 or more. So 2 stars is reachable without finding the one perfect line.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Both twins are needed.** Both twins move in every level's solution. One level (16) needs both twins to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  step on pads on the same move.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Originality claim fails:** mirrored-twin puzzles already exist. The closest I found is [Mirrored\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Pawns](https://gamingonlinux.com/2021/03/puzzle-game-mirrored-pawns-challenges-your-spatial-reasoning-with-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  opposite-movements), which has switchable symmetry. Others are [Mirrored\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Souls](https://hookedgamers.com/pc/mirrored_souls/review/article-2467.html), Mirror Bound and Mirror Match.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The search found nothing with the exact \"stepping on a tile flips the mirror rule\" mechanic, but absence of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  results isn't proof. Please don't advertise it as \"never seen before\". \"A mirror puzzle where the mirror\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  itself is a tile you can step on\" is the honest pitch.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Changed course:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Added a \"stuck\" detector. When no win is reachable, the hint reads \"No way to finish from here — undo\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (Z) or restart\" and the undo button turns red. It never reveals a solution.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Unlocked all levels, so a visitor can try the Axis chapter in the first minute. The stars and level\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  count still show how far you got.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Hardened storage handling and added a fallback for older browsers without `roundRect`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Unchecked:** how the sound and animation feel, and the title screen after the last fix. I saved a copy\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  of the game to `.ambition/steps/4/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
