[613.717, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 5/8 · Range\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What this is really trying to do, as verbs.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Teach a rule without words.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Make a player feel clever.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Let them prove how far they got.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Work in a thumb-sized session on a phone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Keep them from being stuck unknowingly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Fields and the method borrowed from each**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Field | Method borrowed | Direction taken |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Puzzle designer (the genre's own best) | Introduce each element alone in a level that can only be solved\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  using it, then twist it | Already in place and solver-verified. Each chapter's first level contains only the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  new element. No change. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Accessibility / game UX researcher | Run a simulated color-vision-deficiency check, and add reduced-motion\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and mute | Test twin and ring contrast under simulated deuteranopia and protanopia, then add mute and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  reduced motion |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Wordle-style social design (not a field I'd usually consider) | A shareable result should be a compact\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  visual pattern, not a sentence | Share text becomes a per-chapter star grid |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Mobile HCI | Thumb-reach and gesture ergonomics, and blocking browser gestures that fight the game | Swipe\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  anywhere on the game screen and block pull-to-refresh and zoom |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Red team | Corrupt the save data, replay out-of-range state, and check for harm | Run it |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The edge I took:** a visitor sees a result they can paste into a chat in one tap, and the game works for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  people who can't tell teal from amber. Nothing here changes the puzzle itself.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
