[673.46, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step report**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Did:** I borrowed concrete methods from four fields and applied them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Accessibility research:** the orange twin and its goal ring are now rounded squares, and the teal ones\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  stay round. Shape now tells them apart as well as color. I added a mute button on the title screen, saved\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with your progress. Reduced-motion is respected: the screen shake, win burst and pad pulsing are toned down.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Wordle-style sharing:** the share text is now a compact grid you can paste anywhere. It has one row\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  per chapter, with 🟩 for 3 stars, 🟨 for 2, 🟥 for 1 and ⬛ for unplayed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Mobile ergonomics:** you can swipe anywhere on the game screen, and pull-to-refresh and zoom no longer\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fight the game.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Red team:** I tried corrupted saves and 300 rapid key presses.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Color blindness.** Under simulated red-green color blindness, teal and amber had identical brightness\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (contrast 1.00), so only hue told them apart. That is why the shape cue matters.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Corrupted saves crashed the game.** A bad level index or a string in the saved data caused an error.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The save is now checked on load, and all seven corruption cases open cleanly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Harms.** The game has no network use, tracking or dark patterns. The remaining risks are low. The pad\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  glow pulses slowly, below the usual flash-rate limit, and reduced-motion tones it down. Sounds only start\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  after your first input.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Verified:** the solver teaching checks still pass, a Chrome run won all 16 levels with no errors, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  touch swipe from outside the board won level 1, and the 300-key spam produced no errors.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Unchecked:** I haven't tested that the share text lands correctly on a real clipboard, since headless\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Chrome blocks it. I also haven't tried the mute button's actual sound, or the feel of the game.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Changed course:** none. These were additions, and the levels and rules are unchanged. I saved a copy to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/steps/5/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
