[816.688, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step report**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Did:** I built `.ambition/tools/accept.js`, a 19-check acceptance test that isn't me grading myself.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Solver:** it checks the level count, that each solves optimally, and that each chapter's new element\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is needed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Real Chrome:** it plays all 16 levels with real keystrokes. It also checks stars, undo and restart,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  saved progress, the share text, frame time, contrast numbers, and layout at five sizes from 320×568 to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1440×900.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Cold read:** I also dumped every screen's text and read it as a first-time player.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Found:** the first run was 17/19, and both failures were fixable.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A test bug of mine: it checked for the flip pad in the wrong way.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A real layout issue: the top buttons were 37px, below the 40px minimum I set, so they're now 44px.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cold-read fixes:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The level 1 hint was clumsy (\"orange moves the opposite way sideways\") and didn't explain the rule\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  badges. I rewrote it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The pit hint said pits \"swallow\" a twin and also that the move is \"refused\". I made it consistent.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - \"1 moves\" is now \"1 move\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The final win message now breaks onto two lines as intended.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The level header now names the chapter, e.g. \"LEVEL 10 · PITS\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Visual check found a defect the test missed:** in landscape on a phone, the rule badges overlapped the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  board's corner. I fixed it and added that overlap to the test. Final result: 19 of 19 checks pass, zero\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  console errors, a steady 16.6 ms per frame, and a 48 ms load.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Compared with the first version on the same layout checks:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The first version had 35–36 px buttons, no touch controls, and a page scroll in landscape. The final has\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  42–44 px buttons, on-screen arrows, no scrolling, and a board that is 2–3 times taller on phones.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - It also has 16 solver-verified levels instead of 11, plus a title screen, stars and sharing. I found\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  nothing it does worse.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Still unjudged:** I haven't played it as a person, so how it feels to play and how good the sound is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  remain unchecked. The \"never seen before\" mechanic claim is also unproven, as flagged in step 4. A copy is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  saved in `.ambition/steps/6/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[816.819, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 7 of pushing the work further: Stretch. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[830.383, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Target.** The ask was for levels that aren't padded. The measurable version of that is **every object in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  every level is load-bearing**. Removing any single wall, pad or pit must change the optimal solution (a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  different length, or more optimal solutions). That is how designers of tight puzzles like Stephen's Sausage\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Roll work, and the fallback is the current solver-verified set. First I'll measure how far the shipped\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  levels are from the bar.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
