[913.616, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 2 shell commands\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && sed -i.bak 's/\"regen\":\"node gen.js \\&\\& node prune.js\"/\"gen\":\"node gen.js\",\"…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[924.759, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ## Report\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **An original puzzle game:** *Mirror Twins*. You steer two twins at once. The second moves mirrored, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **flip pads** change that mirror rule mid-level.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A browser game as a single page:** it's still one self-contained HTML file. I raised it to a title\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  screen, a chapter map, stars against par and a share button.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Your added goal:** about 16 curated levels in four chapters (Mirror, Flip, Pits, Axis), with no padding.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  It's shareable on itch.io or a portfolio, and the flip pad shows up by level 3.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Better:** it has 16 levels instead of 11, and pars equal the solver optimum. It adds a title screen, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  map with stars, sharing, a stuck warning, mute, and shape cues for color-blind players. The board is 2–3\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  times larger on phones, and buttons are 42–44 px instead of 35–36. Every object in every level is load-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  bearing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Gave up:** nothing I could find. The first version's Prev and Next buttons became the level map.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Check on both:** on the same layout check, the first version had a 35 px minimum button and scrolled in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  landscape. The final has no scrolling and no overlaps.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check:** `accept.js` passes **19/19**. It ran the solver checks, a real Chrome playthrough of all\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  16 levels, a stars test, a share-text test, layout at five sizes, contrast numbers, frame time and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  console-error check. The frame time was 16.6 ms and the load 48 ms, with zero console errors.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch:** every object load-bearing. It reached 64 of 64, up from 66 of 73. The limit: soft-lock-prone\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  levels remain (level 10 has 85 of 155 reachable states unwinnable), and I can't judge how fun the levels\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  are.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`mirror-twins-tools/`:** the page template, rules (`logic.js`), levels, solver, generator, pruner and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `accept.js`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`CLAUDE.md`:** a short note on how to run it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`.claude/commands/check-mirror-twins.md`:** a command that rebuilds and checks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rerun:** `cd mirror-twins-tools && npm i && npm run build && npm run check`. A rebuild reproduces the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  shipped file byte for byte.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions made:** none. You answered every question.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not checked:** how the game feels to play and how the sound is, since I can't play or hear it. The title\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  screen after the last fix, and the share text on a real clipboard, were also not checked.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions left**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **How to present the originality claim.** Mirrored-twin puzzles exist, such as Mirrored Pawns, though I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  found none with tile-flipped rules.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Say \"a mirror puzzle where the mirror is a tile you step on\":* it's honest and still distinctive, but\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  less bold.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Say \"never seen before\":* it's punchier but unproven.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *My pick:* the honest wording. **Owner:** you. **By:** before you post, 2026-11-20.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Whether to redesign soft-lock-heavy levels (10 and 11).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Redesign:* it's friendlier, but costs another generation pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Keep:* the stuck warning and undo already handle it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *My pick:* keep for launch, redesign if playtesters complain. **Owner:** you. **By:** after the first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  playtest.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **The human playtest I couldn't run.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Have two or three people play the first three levels cold:* it's the real test of \"I learned something\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  new\", but needs people.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *Skip it:* it's free, but unproven.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - *My pick:* do it. **Owner:** you. **By:** 2026-11-20.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n"]
